# Summit Rush - BONANZA's course 5 (SPEC.md 128.14.6; its NAME is PEAK,
# 128.14.17 item 1): the long DEMO course, a descent with every prop on it and
# all three balls.  Built for the RUBBER ball; four flags, each naming its
# ball (NO TRAP, `bbcourse.py --selfcheck` item 7).  In order:
#  1. the summit: three steep ramps (r -4, two units a tile) with their
#     throws caught on flat landings, then an ICE chute between bumper rails;
#     flag 0 at its foot;
#  2. A, the WINDMILL's tier: its doorway entered along -y, the tube through
#     the house to B, B's ramp down to the DROP chute onto F.  OPTIONAL: a
#     GLASS pad in an alcove off A opens a staircase of one- and two-unit
#     steps past the windmill and the chute onto F (the GLASS branch: a step
#     taken off a Hop is three units - a shatter, back to flag 0 as rubber);
#  3. F, flag 1, SPRING 1 (768): U1 six units up, two tiles past the spring,
#     where its flight is near its APEX (a soft landing);
#  4. the STEEL pad on U1, the long flat COAST down the screen with the LIFT
#     beside it (its own window, never the windmill's), the LAUNCH cannon over
#     a chasm onto a LEVEL tier (steel lands at lvz 384: no stun); flag 2;
#  5. the GLASS pad and the MOAT BRIDGE, a one-tile plank over the void;
#     flag 3 at its far end;
#  6. SPRING 2 at the end of a walled run-up (glass needs its speed), onto L4
#     at the apex; the glass descent of one-unit steps;
#  7. the RUBBER pad, the short climb to the sand green and the CUP
#     (capture 160).
course PEAK "Summit Rush"
width 64
ball rubber
# 1 the summit: three steep ramps (r -4) and their landings, the ice chute
floor rect  11  7 14 10  flat 36
wall  rect  10  6 15  7  flat 37
wall  rect  10  7 11 10  flat 37
wall  rect  14  7 15 10  flat 37
floor rect  11 10 14 12  ramp y 10 12 36 32
wall  tile  10 10  flat 37
wall  tile  10 11  flat 35
wall  tile  14 10  flat 37
wall  tile  14 11  flat 35
floor rect  11 12 14 15  flat 32
wall  rect  10 12 11 16  flat 33
wall  rect  11 15 14 16  flat 33
floor rect  14 12 16 15  ramp x 14 16 32 28
wall  tile  14 15  flat 33
wall  tile  15 15  flat 31
floor rect  16 12 19 15  flat 28
wall  tile  15 11  flat 31
wall  rect  16 11 20 12  flat 29
wall  rect  19 12 20 15  flat 29
floor rect  16 15 19 21  ramp y 15 21 28 25
surface ice rect 16 15 19 21
wall  rect  15 16 16 21  flat 29
wall  rect  19 15 20 21  flat 29
surface bounce rect 15 16 16 21
surface bounce rect 19 15 20 21
floor rect  16 21 19 23  ramp y 21 23 25 21
wall  tile  15 21  flat 26
wall  tile  15 22  flat 24
wall  tile  19 21  flat 26
wall  tile  19 22  flat 24
# 2 A, the windmill's tier; its house; B; the drop chute to F
floor rect  16 23 25 27  flat 21
checkpoint 18 24 ball rubber
wall  rect  21 19 24 23  flat 27
wall  rect  24 21 25 23  flat 27
tube keep  23 23  24 19  via 23 19
prop windmill 23 23  seed 16
floor rect  24 18 28 20  flat 19
wall  rect  24 17 28 18  flat 20
wall  rect  28 18 29 20  flat 20
floor rect  26 20 28 26  ramp y 20 26 19 16
wall  rect  28 20 29 28  flat 20
floor rect  26 26 28 28  flat 16
wall  rect  25 28 29 30  flat 22
tube drop  26 27  26 30  out +y  height 3
# 2b the OPTIONAL glass branch: a glass pad on A's corner, a staircase of
# one- and two-unit steps past the windmill and the chute onto F
floor rect  22 27 25 28  flat 21
pad glass 23 27
floor rect  22 28 24 29  flat 20
floor rect  22 29 24 30  flat 18
wall  rect  24 28 25 30  flat 22
floor rect  22 30 24 31  flat 17
floor rect  22 31 24 32  flat 15
floor rect  22 32 24 33  flat 14
# 3 F, flag 1, spring 1 up six units to U1
floor rect  24 30 29 35  flat 13
checkpoint 25 32 ball rubber
spring 27 33 768
# 4 U1, the steel pad, the coast and the lift beside it, the LAUNCH over the chasm
floor rect  29 31 34 36  flat 19
pad steel 32 33
floor band  -2 2 66 81  flat 19
wall  band  -4 -3 66 81  flat 20
floor tile 38 35 flat 19
floor tile 39 34 flat 15
floor rect 39 36 41 37 flat 15
floor tile 40 35 flat 15
prop platform 39 35 4
wall rect 39 41 42 42 flat 20
tube launch 40 40 40 42 speed 0 320 384
floor rect 39 42 42 43 flat 19
floor rect 38 45 43 49 flat 19
checkpoint 40 46 ball steel
wall rect 39 49 43 50 flat 20

# 5 the glass pad and the moat bridge
pad glass 40 47
# (the flag at the bridge's head, in the open: inside the moat its pennant and
# pole were behind the moat's front wall - SPEC.md 128.14.25 item 1)
checkpoint 42 48 ball glass
floor rect 43 48 47 49 flat 19
floor rect 47 47 53 50 flat 19
wall rect 47 46 53 47 flat 26
wall rect 47 50 53 51 flat 26
wall rect 49 47 53 48 flat 26
wall rect 49 49 53 50 flat 26
# 6 spring 2 up to L4; the glass descent
spring 51 48 768
floor rect 53 46 57 51 flat 25
wall rect 57 47 58 51 flat 26
floor rect 53 51 57 52 flat 24
floor rect 53 52 57 53 flat 23
floor rect 53 53 57 54 flat 22
floor rect 53 54 57 55 flat 21
# 7 the rubber pad, the short climb, the sand green and the cup
floor rect 53 55 57 57 flat 21
pad rubber 55 56
floor rect 53 57 57 59 ramp y 57 59 21 22
floor rect 53 59 57 62 flat 22
surface sand rect 53 59 57 62
surface normal tile 55 60
cup 55 60
wall rect 52 51 53 63 flat 26
wall rect 57 51 58 63 flat 26
wall rect 53 62 57 63 flat 23

start 12 8

# The autopilot's route (the route demo's and bonanzaperf's leg, 128.14.6):
# the summit's ramps and the chute, flag 0, straight up into the windmill's
# doorway, B, the chute, flag 1, spring 1, the steel pad, the coast, the
# cannon, flag 2, the glass pad, the bridge, flag 3, spring 2, the descent,
# the rubber pad and the cup - no fall (`bbcourse.py --selfcheck` item 8).
way 12  8
way 12 13
way 17 13
way 17 22
